<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92748" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῠᾰδικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυάς</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like diarrhoea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.70
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>suffering from incontinence of urine</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.787
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i>(?) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.7.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>suffering from epiphora</i> or <i>running from the eyes
				without external cause</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dem.Ophth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.46
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοιαδ-</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
